        "explanation": "Explanation:\nHere, P=[2,4,5,1,3,6]P = [2, 4, 5, 1, 3, 6]P=[2,4,5,1,3,6] has 444 ascents (i=1,2,4,5i = 1, 2, 4, 5i=1,2,4,5 satisfy Pi<Pi+1P_i < P_{i + 1}Pi​<Pi+1​). The inverse permutation Q=[4,1,5,2,3,6]Q = [4, 1, 5, 2, 3, 6]Q=[4,1,5,2,3,6] has 222 descents (i=1,3i = 1, 3i=1,3 satisfy Qi>Qi+1Q_i > Q_{i + 1}Qi​>Qi+1​).\nThus, the sum is 666 as required. Finding a permutation with f(P)=7f(P) = 7f(P)=7 would also work."
